; ted-readline-latin1-token-pairs (#374): readline took every byte >= $80
; as the first byte of a token pair and the next byte unchecked as its
; second, also in a text file, where it is a Latin-1 character: an umlaut
; in front of the LF swallowed it and joined the lines.  A text file with
; the lines "; ä" and "; b", loaded under blitz2 (tokenise on), SAVE.
; Correct (the fix): two lines, the umlaut stored as typing stores it (26,
; the germs table); the original saves one line, "; " and the bytes $E4
; $0A with bit 7 cleared by the tokeniser, then "; b".
; @fixed #374
; @file bo.bas "; \xe4\n; b\n"
; @source F bo.bas
; @expect data bo.bas "; \x1a\x00; b\x00"
timeout 10
wait req "OKEE DOKEE"
gad 1
wait screen
menu 0 2
wait freq "Name to save file as"
freq ok
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
